60e9e529e55c5b74645e","date":"2026-09-11T00:01:00+03:00","message":"(chore) O3-5964: Remove unreferenced SCSS files and dead AllergyFormTab component (#3638)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"solomonfortune","authorEmail":"solomonbuwule@gmail.com"},{"hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T23:29:42+03:00","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers are now named 'Edit or delete procedure' and 'Attachment actions', so the specs can no longer find them by 'Options'.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"79767b40a5cc1b1df64b036ddd327c4e7f3d27ec","date":"2026-08-28T22:16:59+03:00","message":"(fix) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#3607)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison\n\n* (fix) Define package-level clean tasks","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"09db7da4c93818faf08a8db1f87e191e465de3eb","date":"2026-08-12T11:22:48+03:00","message":"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#3564)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"22131a77ad06a970b881aca04cc0c3e27e634f07","date":"2026-07-09T17:16:14-04:00","message":"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#3464)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"}],"totalCount":327}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X3tbvqxJ9hwKsn7YcRqXWF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
