{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ESFApCYTgeUCrSkj3nsFm","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"120d22e968d57a1ce47a5a908e50e79f485cfcb1","date":"2026-06-11T15:24:33+03:00","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)","refs":"","body":"The allergy '+' control in the order basket's drug search falls back to\nlaunching the patient chart's allergy form workspace when the host does\nnot provide a launcher. The fill prescription workflow renders the order\nbasket outside the patient chart, so that fallback opened the\npatient-chart workspace group with null group props and crashed every\naction button registered to it with 'Cannot read properties of null\n(reading patientUuid)'.\n\nRegister the exported allergy form workspace from the allergies app into\nthe fill-prescription-window and pass its name as\nallergyFormWorkspaceName in the order basket window props, so the form\nopens as a child of the dispensing app's own workspace window. This is\nthe same wiring the ward app added in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2561 after the form was decoupled\nfrom the chart group in openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3353.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f00d364d277a59729583d2dfbafe965878f0e650","date":"2026-04-24T01:21:01+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5401: Show only drug order panels in the order basket (#743)","refs":"","body":"* feat: Introduce configurable drug order type UUID for filtering visible order panels in the dispensing workflow.\n\n* fixup\n\n* ref: use dynamic drug order type UUID in generateRandomDrugOrder\n\n* Address review feedback\n\n- Revert useConfig in the e2e drug order helper. generateRandomDrugOrder\n  is called from Playwright test.beforeEach, which runs in the Node test\n  process with no React renderer, so useConfig would throw \"Invalid hook\n  call\" at runtime. Restore the hardcoded order type UUID that was in\n  place before 302c162; the e2e suite targets known backend seed data,\n  so a literal UUID is sufficient.\n- Fix a missing space in the drugOrderTypeUUID config description.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"praneeth","authorEmail":"praneeth7077@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fb68bc6920558d89c071c782e8f8c4fa00042b29","date":"2026-01-09T12:39:05-05:00","message":"(feat) O3-5006 add order basket and modal to confirm dispense after order basket submission (#686)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Mark Goodrich <mgoodrich@pih.org>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"}],"totalCount":3}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd29645-34e6-4cd5-9cab-d465499c0f3d","uuid":"31ce69be-be30-4005-91f5-11b8b5e954ca","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:40:52.260Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"120d22e968d57a1ce47a5a908e50e79f485cfcb1","date":"2026-06-11T15:24:33+03:00","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)","refs":"","body":"The allergy '+' control in the order basket's drug search falls back to\nlaunching the patient chart's allergy form workspace when the host does\nnot provide a launcher. The fill prescription workflow renders the order\nbasket outside the patient chart, so that fallback opened the\npatient-chart workspace group with null group props and crashed every\naction button registered to it with 'Cannot read properties of null\n(reading patientUuid)'.\n\nRegister the exported allergy form workspace from the allergies app into\nthe fill-prescription-window and pass its name as\nallergyFormWorkspaceName in the order basket window props, so the form\nopens as a child of the dispensing app's own workspace window. This is\nthe same wiring the ward app added in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2561 after the form was decoupled\nfrom the chart group in openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3353.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f00d364d277a59729583d2dfbafe965878f0e650","date":"2026-04-24T01:21:01+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5401: Show only drug order panels in the order basket (#743)","refs":"","body":"* feat: Introduce configurable drug order type UUID for filtering visible order panels in the dispensing workflow.\n\n* fixup\n\n* ref: use dynamic drug order type UUID in generateRandomDrugOrder\n\n* Address review feedback\n\n- Revert useConfig in the e2e drug order helper. generateRandomDrugOrder\n  is called from Playwright test.beforeEach, which runs in the Node test\n  process with no React renderer, so useConfig would throw \"Invalid hook\n  call\" at runtime. Restore the hardcoded order type UUID that was in\n  place before 302c162; the e2e suite targets known backend seed data,\n  so a literal UUID is sufficient.\n- Fix a missing space in the drugOrderTypeUUID config description.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"praneeth","authorEmail":"praneeth7077@gmail.com"},{"hash":"fb68bc6920558d89c071c782e8f8c4fa00042b29","date":"2026-01-09T12:39:05-05:00","message":"(feat) O3-5006 add order basket and modal to confirm dispense after order basket submission (#686)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Mark Goodrich <mgoodrich@pih.org>","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"}],"totalCount":3}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013ESFApCYTgeUCrSkj3nsFm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
